From 8919eb99de10bf577fdcbbfd865146de1cac3bcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 10:32:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] deploy: marketing site owns / , console moves to
 /console/ ; fix marketing cross-links

The marketing/ site shipped in the previous commit was never wired into
the nginx template, so a deployed VM still served the console at the bare
host root and the landing page was unreachable. This restructures the
shared nginx site (deploy/aws/nginx/yantrafleet.conf.template, used by
both cloud kits):

  /            -> /opt/yantrafleet/marketing (static landing/about/etc)
  /console     -> 302 /console/index.html?supa=..&key=..&site=..
  /console/    -> /opt/yantrafleet/console (same redirect trick as /academy/)
  /academy/ /docs/ /ask /health unchanged

Both boot scripts' closing echo, deploy.sh's help text, and both READMEs
now describe the new layout. Both validate.sh scripts gain checks for it
(and drop the old bare-root redirect assertion, which now must NOT match).

Marketing site fixes found while wiring it up:
  * ../LICENSE, ../CHANGELOG.md, ../CONTRIBUTING.md, ../deploy/*/README.md
    links were always broken (nginx never serves the repo root or deploy/)
    -> point at the GitHub blob URLs instead. ../docs/* links are fine.
  * There was no way to reach the console from the marketing site at
    all: add a "Sign in" nav link and make "Open the console" the hero's
    primary action, both -> /console/.

NOTE for an already-running VM: git pull + install.sh does NOT re-template
nginx; the site file is only regenerated by re-running the boot script
(or the envsubst step from it by hand). See the README update.

